[Themes "h2-retreat,transposition"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "1...g6"]
[Start "orthodox 1.d4"]

1... g6 { Black will put the bishop on g7, where it aims down the long diagonal at d4 and b2. }
2. Bf4 { The usual London bishop. Against the fianchetto it also watches e5, the square Black wants for a pawn break. }
2... Bg7
( 2... Nf6 { Transposes to 1...Nf6 2.Bf4 g6. } )
( 2... d6 3. e3 )
( 2... d5 3. e3 )
( 2... c5 3. e3 )
3. e3 { Supports d4 against the bishop on g7 and opens the bishop on f1. }
3... d6
( 3... Nf6 { Transposes to 1...Nf6 2.Bf4 g6 3.e3 Bg7. } )
( 3... c5 4. c3 { Backs up d4 against the bishop on g7 and the pawn on c5. } 4... Qb6 ( 4... cxd4 5. exd4 ) 5. Qb3 { Offers a queen trade, which takes away the piece hitting b2. } )
( 3... d5 4. Nf3 Nf6 { Transposes to 1...Nf6 2.Bf4 g6 3.e3 Bg7 4.Nf3 d5. } )
4. Nf3
4... Nd7
( 4... Nf6 { Transposes to 1...Nf6 2.Bf4 g6 3.e3 Bg7 4.Nf3 d6. } )
( 4... e5 $2 5. dxe5 dxe5 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 7. Nxe5 { White wins a pawn: if ...Bxe5, the bishop on f4 takes back. } )
( 4... c5 5. c3 )
5. h3 { Gives the bishop h2, so ...e5 does not chase it off the diagonal. }
5... e5 6. Bh2 { The bishop stays on the b8-h2 diagonal and keeps pressing e5. Plan: Be2 or Bc4, castle, and c3 to hold d4. } *
